{
  "packs": [
    "basics",
    "github-actions",
    {
      "id": "grow_with_claudinite",
      "config": { "retention_days": 10 },
      "answers": {
        "retention": "10 days — the recommended rethink window before a captured conversation log is pruned."
      }
    },
    "local_packs/claudinite",
    {
      "id": "local_packs/canon-curation",
      "accept": [
        {
          "rule": "file-placement",
          "path": ".claudinite/local_packs/canon-curation/",
          "reason": "the canon home's curation local pack deliberately shares the checks/ engine lib (findings, lines, context) — the same named cross-cutting concern as the packs/ acceptance; in the home checkout the engine is the repo's own tracked tree, not a consumer mount, so the reach is inherent"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "barriers",
      "answers": {
        "goals": "Keep extending.md's engine/content boundary structural: core (checks/, migrations/, mount/, routines/, .github/, the top-level docs, and the shared engine modules under packs/ and skills/) must never name a specific pack or skill — packs and skills are discovered content, and a core file citing one couples the engine to its content. One rule per namespace (packs/*, skills/*); reviewed inherent couplings live in each rule's except."
      },
      "config": {
        "rules": [
          {
            "from": [
              "checks",
              "migrations",
              "mount",
              "routines",
              ".github",
              "README.md",
              "bootstrap.md",
              "consumer-safe-changes.md",
              "extending.md",
              "packs/registry.mjs",
              "packs/load-active-prose.mjs",
              "packs/env.mjs",
              "packs/interview.mjs",
              "skills/registry.mjs",
              "skills/mount-skills.mjs"
            ],
            "to": "packs/*",
            "matchNames": true,
            "matchUniqueFilenames": false,
            "reason": "core is the engine that runs pack content — it must not name the specific packs it runs (extending.md)",
            "except": [
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/README.md",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): the core .github/ README documents the chrome-extension-release plumbing being vendored out of core (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-daily-release.yml",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release",
                  "packs/github-actions"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): chrome-extension-release reusable release infra hosted in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-publish-store.yml",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): chrome-extension-release reusable release infra hosted in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-release.yml",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension",
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): chrome-extension-release reusable release infra hosted in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": ".github/actions/read-release-config/read-config.mjs",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): a chrome-release composite action in the core .github/ tree; being vendored out (#276)"
              },
              {
                "path": "migrations/active_migrations/2026-07-12-grow-with-claudinite-seed.mjs",
                "to": [
                  "packs/grow_with_claudinite"
                ],
                "reason": "inherent: a one-time seed migration necessarily names the single pack it seeds; it self-retires once the fleet converges"
              },
              {
                "path": "migrations/active_migrations/2026-07-12-tidy-repo-seed.mjs",
                "to": [
                  "packs/tidy-repo"
                ],
                "reason": "inherent: a one-time seed migration necessarily names the single pack it seeds; it self-retires once the fleet converges"
              },
              {
                "path": "migrations/active_migrations/2026-07-13-chrome-release-vendoring.mjs",
                "to": [
                  "packs/chrome-extension-release"
                ],
                "reason": "inherent: a one-time vendoring migration necessarily names the pack whose plumbing it relocates into consumers; it self-retires once the fleet converges"
              },
              {
                "path": "bootstrap.md",
                "to": [
                  "packs/grow_with_claudinite",
                  "packs/tidy-repo"
                ],
                "reason": "inherent(operational seed): the one-time seed one-liner (bootstrap step 4b) backfills these default-on packs into an existing declaration while their self-retiring seed migrations are live; retires with those migrations"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "from": [
              "checks",
              "migrations",
              "mount",
              "routines",
              ".github",
              "README.md",
              "bootstrap.md",
              "consumer-safe-changes.md",
              "extending.md",
              "packs/registry.mjs",
              "packs/load-active-prose.mjs",
              "packs/env.mjs",
              "packs/interview.mjs",
              "skills/registry.mjs",
              "skills/mount-skills.mjs"
            ],
            "to": "skills/*",
            "matchNames": true,
            "matchUniqueFilenames": false,
            "reason": "core is the engine that surfaces skill content — it must not name the specific skills it runs (extending.md)",
            "except": [
              {
                "path": ".github/actions/report-failure/action.yml",
                "to": [
                  "skills/git-github-advanced"
                ],
                "reason": "decouple(release-infra): a chrome-release composite action in the core .github/ tree cites the git/GitHub skill; being vendored out (#276)"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "rules": {},
  "accept": [
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "packs/",
      "reason": "pack check modules deliberately share the checks/ engine lib — a named cross-cutting concern per skills/file-placement/SKILL.md; packs are organized by pack, not by dependency"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "skills/",
      "reason": "a skill's check-the-work modules deliberately share the checks/ engine lib (findings.mjs) — the same named cross-cutting concern as the packs/ acceptance; checks are co-located with the skill whose action they validate, not organized by dependency"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "routines/fleet/plan.mjs",
      "reason": "the core planner deliberately imports the pack-discovery registry (packs/registry.mjs — core machinery per extending.md, not a specific pack) to enumerate each repo's run_daily tasks; discovery lives under packs/ and the planner under routines/, so the cross-tree reach is inherent and correct, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "routines/fleet/signals.mjs",
      "reason": "the member-declaration read deliberately imports the one shared id-extractor (packEntryId in packs/registry.mjs — core machinery per extending.md, not a specific pack) so the fleet's activePacks normalization and the engine can never drift on the declaration forms; the cross-tree reach is inherent, the same as the planner's registry import"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "checks/lib/context.mjs",
      "reason": "the engine's file-set builder deliberately imports the consumer-layout constant SHARED_SUBDIR (beside LOCAL_PACKS_SUBDIR in packs/registry.mjs — core machinery per extending.md, not a specific pack) so the shared-mount sweep exclusion and the vendor writer share one definition; the cross-tree reach is inherent, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "migrations/registry.mjs",
      "reason": "the canon-side migration registry deliberately builds on the vendored sync surface in the engine lib (checks/lib/migrations.mjs — the home pack-independence mandates, since pack checks consult migrationActive and packs import only the engine surface); one definition, re-exported for canon callers, so the cross-tree reach is inherent, not a misplacement"
    },
    {
      "rule": "file-placement",
      "path": "mount/vendor.mjs",
      "reason": "the vendor-set computation deliberately imports the import-surface facts from the engine lib (checks/lib/imports.mjs — the one home the pack-independence check judges against), so \"what a pack may import\" and \"what a vendor set must carry\" share one definition; the cross-tree reach is inherent, not a misplacement"
    }
  ]
}

